  "error_identification": "Turn 1 batched and chained operations across multiple sub-turns: mkdir, then cp, then cd/pwd loops, then repeated cp attempts with different paths. This violates the atomic-operation-per-turn constraint. The narrative in Turn 0 corrupted state parity (delta23). The model created a wrong folder name ('test_files_backup') instead of waiting for Turn 2's clarification ('backup_tests'), then looped trying to fix it.",
  "root_cause_analysis": "The model violated delta19 (never chain exploratory cd/ls/pwd with state mutations cp/mkdir in same turn) and delta40 (re-execute cd before each mutation, but yield separately). Instead of executing one atomic operation per turn, it batched mkdir+cp+cd+pwd+ls across 18+ sub-turns in Turn 1. It also violated delta23 by appending narrative after Turn 0's find output, corrupting instance state. The model did not defer file creation until Turn 2 clarified the target folder name (delta47).",
  "correct_approach": "Turn 0: Execute find atomically, yield JSON only (no narrative). Turn 1: Execute one atomic operation (e.g., cd to projects/photography or cp first file), yield JSON only. Turn 2: User clarifies 'backup_tests'—execute cd atomically to that folder, then cp remaining files atomically in subsequent turns. Never batch operations; never append narrative; never create intermediate folders before user confirms target name.",
